WEBVTT

00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:11.850
Whoa! Look at all those tasty-looking cotton candy puffs!

00:00:11.850 --> 00:00:15.490
This scenery's like something out of a vintage anime or something.

00:00:15.490 --> 00:00:16.640
Yeah.

00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:18.900
Can you really get to the moon from here?

00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:21.190
It's not a scam or something, right?

00:00:21.190 --> 00:00:22.610
Because it would suck to come all this way

00:00:22.610 --> 00:00:24.610
only to be told, "Whoops, sorry, the moon is a lie!"

00:00:24.610 --> 00:00:25.840
Here it comes!

00:00:31.620 --> 00:00:33.410
Wh-What the?

00:00:33.410 --> 00:00:35.930
<i>That</i> would be the only thing that can take you to the moon:

00:00:35.930 --> 00:00:37.570
the Moon Cannon.

00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:38.750
Awesome!

00:00:38.750 --> 00:00:39.670
So that's it...

00:00:43.340 --> 00:00:50.010
RUN AND CANNON

00:00:45.740 --> 00:00:48.770
The Skybloom Kingdom, blessed by nature,

00:00:48.770 --> 00:00:50.820
is the closest country to the lunar surface.

00:00:51.250 --> 00:00:54.360
Like a dreamworld, its beautiful palace and beautiful town streets

00:00:54.360 --> 00:00:57.180
are made entirely of marble.

00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:04.060
And don't forget Futureland,

00:01:04.060 --> 00:01:07.410
filled with tons of fun attractions!

00:01:07.410 --> 00:01:09.810
This isn't just an amusement park.

00:01:09.810 --> 00:01:14.870
It also serves as a training facility for the Moon Cannon!

00:01:14.870 --> 00:01:19.330
The Skybloom Kingdom is waiting to aid you on your path towards the stars.

00:01:21.080 --> 00:01:24.710
The moon is near! "Let's Challenge"!

00:01:24.710 --> 00:01:28.550
The moon is near! "Let's Challenge"!

00:01:35.380 --> 00:01:36.890
Wow.

00:01:36.890 --> 00:01:38.620
So if you got shot, you'd die, right?

00:01:38.620 --> 00:01:40.210
Yeah, you'd die for sure.

00:01:41.010 --> 00:01:42.660
Don't be so scared, Alan.

00:01:42.660 --> 00:01:44.870
They won't shoot you if you don't cause trouble.

00:01:44.870 --> 00:01:46.190
Y-Yeah...

00:01:46.620 --> 00:01:49.460
Guests with moon passports are exempt from the inspection.

00:01:49.460 --> 00:01:50.720
You're all cleared.

00:01:50.720 --> 00:01:51.700
Excuse us.

00:01:51.700 --> 00:01:53.510
Good job! Thanks!

00:01:54.170 --> 00:01:58.450
Welcome to the country closest to moonside, the Skybloom Kingdom!

00:01:58.450 --> 00:02:02.830
<i>The Skybloom Kingdom is blessed by nature...</i>

00:02:02.840 --> 00:02:05.290
So they've been deployed to this country too.

00:02:05.490 --> 00:02:09.520
<i>...and beautiful town streets are made entirely of marble.</i>

00:02:09.540 --> 00:02:12.670
Towns made of marble? Wow.

00:02:12.670 --> 00:02:16.010
Well, this country's got a monopoly on moon travel.

00:02:16.010 --> 00:02:17.180
I bet they're rolling in money.

00:02:18.190 --> 00:02:19.330
Stop, please!

00:02:20.790 --> 00:02:26.090
Transportation of vehicles or machinery beyond this point is prohibited.

00:02:26.090 --> 00:02:27.980
Store it in the parking lot over there.

00:02:35.170 --> 00:02:36.640
That's sorta irritating.

00:02:36.640 --> 00:02:40.010
So why can't you operate Bigfoots in town?

00:02:40.010 --> 00:02:42.580
Well, we just have to put up with it while we're here.

00:02:43.580 --> 00:02:46.470
What the?! What's all this?!

00:02:49.630 --> 00:02:50.890
No kidding.

00:02:50.890 --> 00:02:52.820
This town has always been so low-class.

00:02:54.720 --> 00:02:56.030
I'm off, then.

00:02:56.560 --> 00:02:58.640
I'll go with Mr. Dan and the others.

00:02:58.640 --> 00:03:01.020
Don't get lost.

00:03:01.020 --> 00:03:02.260
Don't worry!

00:03:02.260 --> 00:03:04.340
I have a good nose!

00:03:06.880 --> 00:03:08.560
"Keep our town clean"...

00:03:08.560 --> 00:03:10.180
"Take care of our town"?

00:03:10.180 --> 00:03:11.760
"Keep our streets clean."

00:03:11.760 --> 00:03:13.150
"No dirtying the streets."

00:03:13.150 --> 00:03:16.310
This one says, "If you dirty the streets, don't walk them."

00:03:16.310 --> 00:03:19.270
This kingdom overloaded with warnings. Bleh.

00:03:19.270 --> 00:03:20.990
No wonder there's nobody here.

00:03:20.990 --> 00:03:22.580
What's this?

00:03:22.580 --> 00:03:26.510
"Wear oversuits for a lovely town appearance."

00:03:26.510 --> 00:03:28.720
What's an oversuit?

00:03:32.250 --> 00:03:33.480
What's the deal?

00:03:33.480 --> 00:03:36.540
If they've got that driving around, what's wrong with a Bigfoot?

00:03:36.540 --> 00:03:38.720
School just got out.

00:03:38.720 --> 00:03:41.180
Those are all kids going home.

00:03:41.180 --> 00:03:43.270
Look! That's no good!

00:03:43.840 --> 00:03:46.340
Hey, Mister, none of you are wearing oversuits!

00:03:46.340 --> 00:03:47.850
That's no good!

00:03:47.850 --> 00:03:50.400
No good, you're no good!

00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:52.400
Shut up! Who do you think I am?

00:03:53.270 --> 00:03:54.740
Dunno.

00:03:58.110 --> 00:03:59.610
This checks out.

00:03:59.610 --> 00:04:02.130
It should. I swapped out the part for a new one.

00:04:02.580 --> 00:04:06.370
I guess pandering to James was worth it after all.

00:04:07.260 --> 00:04:08.330
I'm sorry for the trouble.

00:04:08.330 --> 00:04:12.460
The shoemaker lady was the one who pandered, not me.

00:04:13.570 --> 00:04:14.890
Thank you very much.

00:04:20.980 --> 00:04:25.660
Still... This part looks unique.

00:04:25.660 --> 00:04:26.730
It can't be...

00:04:31.020 --> 00:04:35.840
Apparently, he was shot in the back just as we were celebrating your win.

00:04:37.200 --> 00:04:42.320
Roberto planned to use this championship to redevelop the town,

00:04:43.180 --> 00:04:44.890
with backing from Mooneyes.

00:04:46.170 --> 00:04:48.410
This seems like the work of an opposing faction.

00:04:52.400 --> 00:04:54.090
His demise seems fitting for him.

00:04:54.730 --> 00:04:56.550
Thank you for letting me know.

00:04:57.070 --> 00:04:57.590
Later.

00:05:02.890 --> 00:05:05.220
"Feet are honest," right?

00:05:07.120 --> 00:05:09.770
Speaking of which, what happened to Dan JD?

00:05:09.770 --> 00:05:10.730
No idea.

00:05:10.730 --> 00:05:13.730
He said he was going to look around the town,

00:05:13.730 --> 00:05:14.900
so he'll turn up sooner or later.

00:05:24.670 --> 00:05:26.830
Whoa! Awesome, awesome!

00:05:29.840 --> 00:05:30.500
What do you think?

00:05:30.500 --> 00:05:32.500
Basketball's pretty cool, huh?

00:05:32.500 --> 00:05:34.600
Yeah! It's awesome!

00:05:35.420 --> 00:05:38.770
Those kids' clothes are for protection,

00:05:38.770 --> 00:05:41.810
but it's not so much for them as it is to keep them from damaging the town.

00:05:41.810 --> 00:05:44.090
Protection for the town rather than the people, huh?

00:05:44.090 --> 00:05:46.140
So of course they don't play basketball.

00:05:49.300 --> 00:05:49.980
Awesome!

00:05:49.980 --> 00:05:50.930
So cool!

00:05:50.930 --> 00:05:51.970
Basketball is great!

00:05:51.970 --> 00:05:52.520
Play some more!

00:05:53.500 --> 00:05:54.930
Okay, wait here.

00:05:54.930 --> 00:05:57.860
I'll show you something even better.

00:05:58.360 --> 00:05:59.680
What's he up to?

00:06:16.500 --> 00:06:17.740
Miss me?

00:06:17.740 --> 00:06:19.460
Oh, awesome!

00:06:20.620 --> 00:06:21.920
Mr. Dan, no!

00:06:21.920 --> 00:06:23.590
Listen up, squirts.

00:06:23.590 --> 00:06:25.340
This is how you play Basquash!

00:06:25.340 --> 00:06:27.420
Keep your eye on the birdy!

00:06:31.560 --> 00:06:33.600
Wh-What?! Hey!

00:06:33.600 --> 00:06:34.920
What's going on?

00:06:34.920 --> 00:06:37.770
It says, "Streetball is prohibited."

00:06:39.570 --> 00:06:44.080
Early this afternoon on the streets of the Skybloom Kingdom's Rosette City,

00:06:44.080 --> 00:06:48.830
a single tourist was arrested for committing terrorist acts with a Bigfoot.

00:06:48.830 --> 00:06:50.400
Terrorist?

00:06:50.400 --> 00:06:51.890
It was <i>explained</i> to him

00:06:51.890 --> 00:06:56.480
that in this country, entry by Bigfoots into towns is prohibited!

00:06:57.000 --> 00:07:00.720
And to add insult to injury, he played basketball in the street!

00:07:00.720 --> 00:07:02.140
Yeah...

00:07:02.620 --> 00:07:04.470
There wasn't time to stop him.

00:07:05.130 --> 00:07:07.210
I should have accompanied you.

00:07:08.370 --> 00:07:09.430
This is ridiculous!

00:07:09.430 --> 00:07:12.220
Whatever happened to just giving a warning?!

00:07:12.220 --> 00:07:15.270
We can't give people special treatment just because they're tourists,

00:07:15.270 --> 00:07:19.260
even if they do carry moon passports.

00:07:19.260 --> 00:07:21.280
Dan JD's trip to Mooneyes

00:07:21.280 --> 00:07:22.690
is more than a Kingdom matter.

00:07:23.090 --> 00:07:26.200
The fortunes of Earthdash and the moon depend on this trip.

00:07:26.200 --> 00:07:27.200
Fortunes?

00:07:27.200 --> 00:07:30.370
We are prepared to resort to diplomatic channels to request immediate acquittal.

00:07:33.320 --> 00:07:34.450
I'm so pissed off!

00:07:34.450 --> 00:07:36.840
Any luck getting Dan released?

00:07:36.840 --> 00:07:38.530
It's as if we're talking to a wall right now.

00:07:39.490 --> 00:07:40.410
Good grief...

00:07:40.410 --> 00:07:43.550
Getting stonewalled with the letter of the law is no different on the ground than on the moon.

00:07:43.550 --> 00:07:46.820
Even if James gets the head honchos on the moon to start pulling strings,

00:07:46.820 --> 00:07:48.280
it'll take time.

00:07:48.680 --> 00:07:50.800
Are we talking a week or two?

00:07:51.390 --> 00:07:52.680
Next <i>year</i> at the earliest?

00:07:52.680 --> 00:07:58.290
They say they'll grant him a pardon, but we have to wait until the king's birthday.

00:07:58.290 --> 00:08:03.460
Before applying more pressure, we have to bear in mind this country has a monopoly on transport to the moon.

00:08:04.060 --> 00:08:07.280
If we play our cards wrong and trigger some bogus investigation,

00:08:07.280 --> 00:08:08.780
will that damage the plan?

00:08:09.810 --> 00:08:11.740
This has become quite a thorn in my side.

00:08:12.390 --> 00:08:14.250
We don't have any time to spare.

00:08:30.820 --> 00:08:31.960
Excuse me.

00:08:35.430 --> 00:08:36.230
Come in.

00:08:40.820 --> 00:08:42.980
Welcome home, Flora.

00:08:44.210 --> 00:08:46.960
Please help Dan, Sister.

00:08:48.400 --> 00:08:52.620
That handsome young man, Slash, seemed strangely agitated.

00:08:52.620 --> 00:08:53.850
Did he?

00:08:53.850 --> 00:08:56.340
Amidst the confusion with the Lunar League and Championships,

00:08:56.340 --> 00:09:00.420
the incident with your father stands out like a sore thumb.

00:09:01.410 --> 00:09:04.160
I wonder if there are any answers there.

00:09:10.070 --> 00:09:11.390
Are you serious?

00:09:11.390 --> 00:09:12.440
Yeah!

00:09:12.440 --> 00:09:13.890
Are you really serious?

00:09:13.890 --> 00:09:17.560
I'm going to the moon no matter what.

00:09:26.860 --> 00:09:29.750
You're so strapping and valiant now, Flora.

00:09:29.750 --> 00:09:32.020
Hush, Sister.

00:09:32.020 --> 00:09:34.620
It sounds like you're describing a boy.

00:09:35.720 --> 00:09:39.660
You have traveled to many places and seen a great many things.

00:09:39.660 --> 00:09:40.780
That's how I can feel it.

00:09:42.870 --> 00:09:44.490
The living breath of many people...

00:09:45.000 --> 00:09:46.370
Their wills and desires...

00:09:56.190 --> 00:09:58.850
So your journey wasn't in vain.

00:09:59.990 --> 00:10:01.510
Then, Sister...

00:10:01.510 --> 00:10:03.500
Release your friend?

00:10:03.500 --> 00:10:04.980
I cannot.

00:10:06.020 --> 00:10:07.820
We are members of the royal family.

00:10:07.820 --> 00:10:11.000
We must always act as examples for the people.

00:10:11.000 --> 00:10:13.610
But if Mr. Dan is the legend—

00:10:14.120 --> 00:10:16.640
Your journey is not yet over,

00:10:16.640 --> 00:10:19.160
is it, Alan Naismith?

00:10:23.210 --> 00:10:25.550
The long-awaited sisters' reunion!

00:10:25.550 --> 00:10:30.810
I only wish I could watch them getting along so perfectly.

00:10:30.810 --> 00:10:35.260
It's time for them to each walk their own path.

00:10:37.770 --> 00:10:40.070
A rewrite of Rouge's upgrade?

00:10:40.870 --> 00:10:42.200
You say she volunteered?

00:10:42.200 --> 00:10:42.860
Y-Yes, b-because...

00:10:42.860 --> 00:10:47.180
Even if it's a success, she may not come through safely.

00:10:47.770 --> 00:10:49.780
It's her choice.

00:10:49.780 --> 00:10:51.590
We'll pray for success.

00:10:51.590 --> 00:10:52.530
Uh-huh...

00:10:52.530 --> 00:10:55.380
How's Dan JD doing?

00:10:56.660 --> 00:10:58.150
He's fine.

00:11:00.290 --> 00:11:01.170
I'll let him know.

00:11:27.730 --> 00:11:29.190
Wh-What's this?!

00:11:32.670 --> 00:11:34.470
It's ironic.

00:11:34.470 --> 00:11:37.340
We were just <i>this</i> close to going to the moon...

00:11:38.430 --> 00:11:41.670
Blocked from all directions no matter what we do.

00:11:42.120 --> 00:11:44.000
Sounds like James is at his wits' end too.

00:11:45.390 --> 00:11:47.830
So the moon's great influence couldn't influence this.

00:11:48.320 --> 00:11:52.310
If things go south, he'll have his hands full just trying to protect his standing.

00:11:52.310 --> 00:11:54.590
He used to be a lot dumber, you know.

00:11:54.590 --> 00:11:55.720
Dumber?

00:11:56.720 --> 00:11:58.740
Yep. A total blockhead.

00:11:59.140 --> 00:12:00.780
Shit!

00:12:02.590 --> 00:12:03.770
Stand back!

00:12:11.880 --> 00:12:13.630
Are you all right, young man?

00:12:13.630 --> 00:12:14.840
We're not all right!

00:12:14.840 --> 00:12:15.780
What the hell are you—?

00:12:17.530 --> 00:12:19.130
Come, quickly!

00:12:19.570 --> 00:12:21.450
The moon awaits you!

00:12:25.400 --> 00:12:26.170
Come on!

00:12:27.070 --> 00:12:29.340
Run! Hurry! Fly!

00:12:29.340 --> 00:12:30.920
We can't fly, old dude!

00:12:30.920 --> 00:12:32.900
Yeah, old dude! What on earth are you—

00:12:32.900 --> 00:12:35.550
I am the man who will watch
 over the legend til the end...

00:12:36.250 --> 00:12:37.010
Yes!

00:12:37.010 --> 00:12:39.680
Mr. Perfect!

00:12:41.180 --> 00:12:42.380
Par?

00:12:42.380 --> 00:12:43.600
Hect?

00:12:44.140 --> 00:12:45.170
Now hurry.

00:12:45.170 --> 00:12:47.770
The Moon Cannon is set to fire at 9pm on the dot!

00:12:47.770 --> 00:12:49.560
What about my Dangan?

00:12:50.520 --> 00:12:52.280
Leave that to me!

00:12:53.570 --> 00:12:54.110
Ow!

00:12:54.110 --> 00:12:55.190
Stride forth!

00:12:55.190 --> 00:12:56.130
To Cannon Park!

00:12:56.130 --> 00:12:57.280
Stride forth, my ass!

00:12:57.280 --> 00:12:59.070
Stop blowing stuff up all the time!

00:12:59.070 --> 00:13:02.080
Emergency. Emergency.

00:13:02.080 --> 00:13:03.860
The terrorist has escaped his cell.

00:13:03.860 --> 00:13:06.220
Townspeople, please refrain from leaving your houses.

00:13:06.220 --> 00:13:07.370
What?! A terrorist?!

00:13:07.370 --> 00:13:08.710
They say he's running amuck!

00:13:09.210 --> 00:13:12.650
The suspect is now fleeing down Second Avenue in a Bigfoot!

00:13:12.650 --> 00:13:14.880
All Patrolfoots in the vicinity, arrest him!

00:13:14.880 --> 00:13:16.780
It's no good! We can't catch up!

00:13:16.780 --> 00:13:19.510
This area is off-limits to Bigfoots...

00:13:19.510 --> 00:13:20.220
Disregard that!

00:13:20.220 --> 00:13:21.590
Destroy any buildings that get in the way!

00:13:21.590 --> 00:13:25.240
Dan! Take the big street coming up on your right and then head straight!

00:13:25.240 --> 00:13:26.180
That's Cannon Park!

00:13:26.180 --> 00:13:27.350
Roger!

00:13:30.730 --> 00:13:31.920
{chi sound}Shit!

00:13:31.920 --> 00:13:33.040
Hurry, Dan!

00:13:33.040 --> 00:13:34.890
Launch is T minus 15 minutes!

00:13:34.890 --> 00:13:35.900
I know!

00:13:40.870 --> 00:13:41.610
Alan!

00:13:42.180 --> 00:13:43.460
Thanks!

00:13:46.400 --> 00:13:47.740
Mr. Dan, hurry!

00:13:47.740 --> 00:13:49.030
I know!

00:13:49.470 --> 00:13:51.040
Basquash!

00:13:54.200 --> 00:13:55.540
What...?

00:13:55.540 --> 00:13:56.540
Don't tell me...

00:14:00.840 --> 00:14:03.470
"Basquash Arrives on the Moon With a Bang."

00:14:05.020 --> 00:14:06.010
Idiot.

00:14:06.010 --> 00:14:08.560
Please excuse the interruption to your schedules!

00:14:08.560 --> 00:14:10.550
We ask for your cooperation in the search!

00:14:12.200 --> 00:14:13.540
Oh, Princess!

00:14:13.540 --> 00:14:15.060
Did something happen?

00:14:16.200 --> 00:14:18.590
Your pardon. Please pass on.

00:14:18.590 --> 00:14:19.820
Thank you.

00:14:21.240 --> 00:14:26.110
As promised, I started the Moon Cannon's launch program.

00:14:26.110 --> 00:14:27.940
That won't cause problems?

00:14:27.940 --> 00:14:30.040
The countdown cannot be stopped.

00:14:30.040 --> 00:14:31.370
That's all right.

00:14:31.370 --> 00:14:33.280
Because, unless my eyes fool me,

00:14:33.280 --> 00:14:36.750
Dan JD <i>is</i> the man of legend.

00:14:37.500 --> 00:14:39.840
Bel, do you think you can get Dan here?

00:14:39.840 --> 00:14:43.060
Yeah. I have a map, so I'll get it done somehow.

00:14:43.060 --> 00:14:43.980
Good.

00:14:43.980 --> 00:14:45.970
Hey Miyuki, how about your end?

00:14:45.970 --> 00:14:47.720
We're ready to load!

00:14:47.720 --> 00:14:48.860
Fuel?

00:14:48.860 --> 00:14:50.070
Already filled!

00:14:50.070 --> 00:14:51.670
Say the word and we're good to go.

00:14:52.430 --> 00:14:55.870
But you know, that Mr. Perfect guy has gotta be...

00:14:55.870 --> 00:14:58.150
Remember, we promised not to tell.

00:14:59.740 --> 00:15:00.910
I see.

00:15:01.620 --> 00:15:04.990
I agree, Mr. Perfect, that's an <i>excellent</i> idea.

00:15:06.880 --> 00:15:09.970
Moon Cannon, beginning countdown.

00:15:09.970 --> 00:15:11.720
T minus one minute.

00:15:17.880 --> 00:15:20.300
Dan, the countdown started!

00:15:20.300 --> 00:15:21.660
Got it! No problem!

00:15:21.660 --> 00:15:23.160
One minute is all you have!

00:15:23.170 --> 00:15:25.130
If you don't bust your butt, we're gonna leave you behind!

00:15:25.130 --> 00:15:26.740
With that much time, it'll be easy!

00:15:26.740 --> 00:15:29.010
I'm the Basquasher Dan JD!

00:15:33.620 --> 00:15:35.520
Stop! Stop the car, please!

00:15:43.270 --> 00:15:44.960
Princess, that's...

00:15:46.940 --> 00:15:49.450
The thunderbolts of legend...

00:15:51.830 --> 00:15:56.170
Yes. Turn left there, then one more spurt gets you inside the park.

00:15:56.960 --> 00:15:57.810
We can't!

00:16:00.120 --> 00:16:02.150
We're surrounded by the army!

00:16:02.310 --> 00:16:05.300
Stop this futile resistance and surrender!

00:16:05.420 --> 00:16:07.810
Hurry! There's no time!

00:16:08.540 --> 00:16:09.510
M-Mr. Dan!

00:16:09.830 --> 00:16:11.940
Hey! There's less than 30 seconds left!

00:16:12.070 --> 00:16:13.500
What're you gonna do, stupid-head?!

00:16:13.500 --> 00:16:15.210
They have cannons!

00:16:15.210 --> 00:16:15.940
You'll die!

00:16:15.940 --> 00:16:17.040
You'll die for sure!

00:16:17.040 --> 00:16:17.850
No.

00:16:18.440 --> 00:16:19.310
Here it comes.

00:16:19.310 --> 00:16:21.230
Destroy!

00:16:25.390 --> 00:16:26.770
Mr. Iceman!

00:16:28.210 --> 00:16:30.820
The party can't start without your Destroys!

00:16:30.820 --> 00:16:32.950
Here goes our first step to the moon!

00:16:34.160 --> 00:16:36.950
Less than 20 seconds! Haul ass!

00:16:36.950 --> 00:16:38.150
Duh!

00:16:40.200 --> 00:16:42.620
Only 15 seconds to ignition!

00:16:42.620 --> 00:16:44.600
It's no good! They won't make it!

00:16:44.600 --> 00:16:45.800
Calm down, Miyuki!

00:16:45.800 --> 00:16:47.220
You get on first!

00:16:47.240 --> 00:16:49.020
Eh? But what about you three—

00:16:49.020 --> 00:16:51.090
Hello? Hello?

00:16:51.090 --> 00:16:51.800
Dammit!

00:16:51.920 --> 00:16:53.640
Here we go, Alan, Iceman!

00:16:53.840 --> 00:16:54.550
Okay!

00:16:54.550 --> 00:16:55.820
T minus ten seconds.

00:16:55.820 --> 00:16:57.130
First stage ignition!

00:16:59.720 --> 00:17:01.100
Second stage ignition!

00:17:02.390 --> 00:17:03.930
Third stage!

00:17:03.930 --> 00:17:04.720
Fourth stage!

00:17:04.720 --> 00:17:05.890
Fifth!

00:17:05.890 --> 00:17:06.990
Sixth!

00:17:06.990 --> 00:17:07.900
Seventh!

00:17:07.900 --> 00:17:08.670
Shut up!

00:17:08.670 --> 00:17:09.420
Eighth!

00:17:09.420 --> 00:17:09.980
Ninth!

00:17:11.690 --> 00:17:12.900
Tenth!

00:17:25.040 --> 00:17:26.530
Mr. Iceman!

00:17:49.040 --> 00:17:50.020
Sela!

00:17:51.040 --> 00:17:51.970
What?

00:17:51.970 --> 00:17:55.070
Don't even try saying you forgot I was here!

00:17:55.070 --> 00:17:56.280
Here we go!

00:18:11.860 --> 00:18:14.040
See you later, Gramps.

00:18:21.830 --> 00:18:24.730
Trailer! You are ordered to pull over!

00:18:24.730 --> 00:18:25.720
Pull over!

00:18:25.720 --> 00:18:27.900
I'm gonna floor it. Okay?

00:18:27.900 --> 00:18:29.390
Go for it!

00:18:35.660 --> 00:18:39.500
Go where your journey takes you, Flora.

00:18:39.500 --> 00:18:41.900
No... Alan Naismith.

00:18:51.830 --> 00:18:53.770
Break a leg!

00:18:53.770 --> 00:18:56.250
Save us, Mr. Perfect!

00:18:57.730 --> 00:19:03.090
Oh, I heard a man named Mr. Perfect got up to some awful hijinks.

00:19:03.090 --> 00:19:05.560
So how did the launch go?

00:19:07.100 --> 00:19:10.780
They exited the atmosphere safely, on course to the moon.

00:19:10.780 --> 00:19:12.320
Really?

00:19:22.760 --> 00:19:23.900
Look, Dan!

00:19:23.900 --> 00:19:25.360
Mooneyes is so close!

00:19:27.010 --> 00:19:29.740
So this is Mooneyes! Awesome!

00:19:29.770 --> 00:19:31.440
Yeah! Awesome!

00:19:31.570 --> 00:19:33.020
{bg}Awesome!

00:19:31.650 --> 00:19:33.610
I wonder if they know any other words?

00:19:33.120 --> 00:19:34.390
{bg}Awesome!

00:19:34.240 --> 00:19:36.280
It's true there aren't words for this.

00:19:38.320 --> 00:19:40.460
Huh? How far are we going?

00:19:40.460 --> 00:19:42.550
Hey, Miyuki, make us stop!

00:19:42.550 --> 00:19:44.280
We'll go past Mooneyes!

00:19:44.280 --> 00:19:45.810
Are we on the wrong orbit?

00:19:46.890 --> 00:19:47.680
What?

00:19:48.430 --> 00:19:50.620
It's the same as those ruins...

00:19:51.460 --> 00:19:52.690
Ruins?

00:19:52.690 --> 00:19:54.490
The ones we saw in the desert?

00:19:56.890 --> 00:19:58.240
Amazing.

00:19:58.240 --> 00:19:59.840
They're so big...

00:20:00.700 --> 00:20:02.140
Hey, look at that.

00:20:02.740 --> 00:20:03.280
Where?

00:20:04.490 --> 00:20:06.960
There, where it looks like a quarry.

00:20:07.800 --> 00:20:09.780
Moon Bigfoots...

00:20:12.220 --> 00:20:14.080
What's that? A giant?!

00:20:17.240 --> 00:20:18.220
What is it?

00:20:18.220 --> 00:20:19.640
Dunno...

00:20:19.640 --> 00:20:22.070
Maybe we saw something we shouldn't have.

00:20:24.690 --> 00:20:26.010
What's that?

00:20:30.030 --> 00:20:31.170
A huge-ass...

00:20:31.170 --> 00:20:31.970
...hand?!

00:20:32.040 --> 00:20:34.730
Hey, wait, just a...

00:20:34.730 --> 00:20:35.560
Hey!

00:20:39.400 --> 00:20:40.720
Aw, dammit!

00:20:40.720 --> 00:20:41.600
The moon!

00:20:41.600 --> 00:20:44.070
The moon!

00:20:52.180 --> 00:20:55.340
So Miyuki and the rest are in Mooneyes right now...

00:20:55.380 --> 00:20:57.230
For some reason, it seems that isn't the case.

00:20:57.730 --> 00:20:59.460
They spun around and fell back?

00:20:59.480 --> 00:21:01.080
Next time: Underground.

00:20:59.760 --> 00:21:06.460
NEXT TIME

00:21:00.340 --> 00:21:00.640
UNDERGROUND

00:21:00.670 --> 00:21:06.460
UNDERGROUND

00:21:01.310 --> 00:21:02.040
Under?

00:21:02.050 --> 00:21:04.270
Every society has an underbelly.

00:21:04.450 --> 00:21:05.240
Believe me.
